Ascii counter Cars:

Strengths:

Centroid tracker – simple, yet effective for basic vehicle tracking in scenes without heavy overlap.

ASCII highway zone – a very creative solution to define the region of interest; you can precisely “draw” the part of the road that the counter observes.

Unique counting per vehicle – each vehicle is counted only once per line, and new vehicles passing through the same point are correctly counted.

Visual feedback – centroids are displayed, vehicle IDs are visible, and lines are clearly marked.

Scalable and flexible – easy to add new lines or modify the ASCII zone mask.

Limitations / Possible Improvements:

Centroid tracker is basic – in traffic congestion (overlapping vehicles), there may be ID loss or multiple vehicles may be merged into a single ID.

No speed or direction filtering – in the current system, vehicles moving backward or stopping may not be classified accurately.

ASCII mask is static – it does not adapt to curves, perspective changes, or shadows.

Performance – with high resolutions and many vehicles, Python + OpenCV without optimization can be slow.

No vehicle classification – currently counts only “vehicle centroids” without distinguishing types (car, truck, motorcycle…).
